** Probe: which exponent spellings STODBL reads. EMISUNIT 1e+06 (Python's
** "%.6g" of 1e6) was E208, as were 1E6 and 1e6; 1.e+06, 1.0e6, 1.0E+06
** and 1000000 were accepted. STODBL wants a decimal point in the
** mantissa before an exponent, so pyaermod writes one (sources._aermod_number).
CO STARTING
   TITLEONE  oracle 14: EMISUNIT factor with a decimal-point mantissa
   MODELOPT  CONC  FLAT  DFAULT
   AVERTIME  1
   POLLUTID  SO2
   RUNORNOT  NOT
CO FINISHED

SO STARTING
   LOCATION  STACK1  POINT  0.0  0.0  0.0
   SRCPARAM  STACK1  500.0  65.00  425.  15.0  5.
   EMISUNIT  1.0e+06  GRAMS/SEC  MICROGRAMS/M**3
   SRCGROUP  ALL
SO FINISHED

RE STARTING
   DISCCART  500.0  500.0  0.0
RE FINISHED

ME STARTING
   SURFFILE  AERMET2.SFC
   PROFFILE  AERMET2.PFL
   SURFDATA  14735  1988
   UAIRDATA  14735  1988
   PROFBASE  0.0  METERS
ME FINISHED

OU STARTING
